  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added strict interior `span_reach` to `HolderProfile` in `crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs` and switched `enclose` to it. A holder band starting at `shank_top` (like the #2180 cone) no longer widens `shank_d`, while a band strictly inside `(flute_len, shank_top)` still widens `enclose`'s single-cylinder fallback for single-cylinder callers.\n- Added `camcraft_tools::neck::shank_with_body` in `crates/tools/src/neck.rs`. When a holder band reaches inside `(flute_len, shank_top)`, it partitions that span across the boundaries of the stated shank (or drawn neck) and the holder body, taking the wider radius on every sub-span.\n- Tightened `HolderStack::shank_bands`'s `beside` boundary check in `crates/tools/src/neck.rs` by `1e-9` mm so floating-point dust at a split foot does not smear the holder radius below the foot.\n- Passed `shank_with_body(&stored, body.as_ref(), neck)` from `crates/app/src/operation/tool_gate.rs` (`job_tool`) and `crates/app/src/fixture_struck.rs` (`op_hits`). `pocket_reach`, `verify`, fixture checks, and the post gate now judge the stated shank below a beside-shank holder foot and still block on real holder collisions from the foot upward.\n- Added decision note `docs/decisions/2199-holder-beside-shank.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo bugs compounded when a holder started at or below `shank_top`:\n1. `HolderProfile::enclose` called inclusive `reach_over(fl, shank_top)`, so a holder starting at `shank_top` widened `judged.shank_d` (#2180).\n2. `job_tool` and `op_hits` discarded `stored.shank_d` once `tool_body::judged` replaced `tool` with the enclosed cylinder, leaving `neck` empty and causing `pocket_reach`, `verify`, fixture checks, and `post` to judge the holder diameter all the way down to `flute_len` (#2199).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins (red before fix, green after fix):\n  - `holder_profile::tests::a_band_touching_only_the_shank_top_does_not_widen_the_judged_shank` (`camcraft-tools`)\n  - `neck::tests::shank_with_body_splits_only_above_a_holder_foot_beside_the_shank`, `shank_with_body_keeps_neck_untouched_when_holder_starts_at_shank_top`, `shank_with_body_never_shrinks_stated_shank_or_neck` (`camcraft-tools`)\n  - `crates/app/tests/tool_body_beside_shank.rs` (`t31_holder_beside_shank_allows_3d_pocket_below_holder_foot_and_refuses_at_foot`, `t31_verify_judges_shank_at_6_35_below_38_1_and_catches_real_holder_hit`, `t31_fixture_law_judges_shank_below_holder_foot_and_catches_holder_beside_shank`, `issue_2180_cone_touching_only_shank_top_never_widens_shank`, `holder_narrower_than_stated_shank_never_shrinks_shank_judgement`)\n- Mutation checks:\n  - Reverted `crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs` to `upstream/main`: `a_band_touching_only_the_shank_top_does_not_widen_the_judged_shank` failed (`left: 60.0`, `right: 6.0`); passed after restore.\n  - Reverted `crates/app/src/operation/tool_gate.rs` to `upstream/main`: `t31_holder_beside_shank_allows_3d_pocket_below_holder_foot_and_refuses_at_foot` and `t31_verify_judges_shank_at_6_35_below_38_1_and_catches_real_holder_hit` failed; both passed after restore.\n  - Reverted `crates/app/src/fixture_struck.rs` to `upstream/main`: `t31_fixture_law_judges_shank_below_holder_foot_and_catches_holder_beside_shank` failed; passed after restore.\n  - Removed `- 1e-9` boundary tolerance in `HolderStack::shank_bands`'s `beside` check: `shank_with_body_splits_only_above_a_holder_foot_beside_the_shank` failed (`r: 17.5` smeared down to `14.478`); passed after restore.\n- Suites and checks run after final Rust edit:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed (`wall 0.7 min, 2 step(s), 0 failed`).\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` (with `RUSTC_WRAPPER` unset because `sccache` 0.19.0 fails on `clippy-driver`): passed with zero warnings.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim`: passed (`camcraft-tools` 88 unit + 11 integration; `camcraft-sim` exited 0).\n  - Targeted `camcraft-app` binaries (`holder_library`, `machine_default_holder`, `mcp_verify`, `pocket3d_reach`, `tool_body_bands`, `tool_body_beside_shank`, `tool_body_drill_probe`, `tool_body_judged`, `tool_neck_laws`): all passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Full `camcraft-ui` build, snapshot PNG lane, and full `cargo xtask gate batch` did not run; only `gate quick`, `camcraft-tools`, `camcraft-sim`, targeted `camcraft-app` integration tests, and clippy on touched crates ran.\n- `crates/app/src/sim_tool_body.rs` (3D viewport outline) was left untouched to avoid conflicting with PR #2179.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2140 touches the same file `crates/app/src/operation/tool_gate.rs` in a different function (`tool_problem` vs `job_tool`); whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Judge the stated shank below a holder foot drawn beside it in 3D reach preflight, verification, fixture checks, and post gating.\nFixes #2199\n",
